    Fix crash that prevented routes from loading on mobile and web
    
    expo-symbols is an iOS-only native package not included in Expo Go or web.
    The non-iOS icon-symbol fallback imported it at runtime (via a plain import),
    and _layout.tsx had an unused IconSymbol import that triggered the same chain.
    Both caused the root layout to crash before any routes could register,
    showing the "Welcome to Expo" placeholder instead of the app.
    
    - Remove unused IconSymbol import from app/_layout.tsx
    - Change expo-symbols import to `import type` so Babel erases it at compile
      time and the native module is never required on non-iOS platforms
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>

